{"unitId":"blue-1","x":1960,"y":1680,"facingDeg":0,"formation":"line","strength":600,"morale":80,"fatigue":0,"ammo":100,"status":"active","continuing":{"kind":"hold"},"orders":[],"account":"Col. Aubry had no orders and held his line south of the bridge. Nothing of the enemy was in sight."},
{"unitId":"blue-2","x":2140,"y":1680,"facingDeg":0,"formation":"line","strength":550,"morale":75,"fatigue":0,"ammo":100,"status":"active","continuing":{"kind":"hold"},"orders":[],"account":"Col. Delacroix had no orders and held his line. Nothing of the enemy was in sight."},
{"unitId":"blue-3","x":1100,"y":1620,"facingDeg":0,"formation":"line","strength":200,"morale":85,"fatigue":2,"ammo":100,"status":"active","continuing":{"kind":"hold"},"orders":[{"orderId":"b3-4","result":"carried-out"}],"account":"Maj. Verneuil edged his squadron up to the river bank and posted vedettes to watch the northern wood across the water. The wood lies more than 700 m off and its edge shows nothing: no movement could be made out among the trees. He has nothing to report but an empty treeline."},
{"unitId":"red-1","x":1950,"y":300,"facingDeg":180,"formation":"line","strength":650,"morale":80,"fatigue":0,"ammo":100,"status":"active","continuing":{"kind":"hold"},"orders":[{"orderId":"r1-4","result":"carried-out"}],"account":"Col. Brandt, though he would rather advance, stood his battalion in line by the road with colours uncased, in plain view for any enemy who came near enough to look."},
{"unitId":"red-2","x":950,"y":820,"facingDeg":200,"formation":"column","strength":650,"morale":70,"fatigue":14,"ammo":100,"status":"active","continuing":{"kind":"hold"},"orders":[{"orderId":"r2-4","result":"carried-out"}],"account":"Col. Hartmann marched as ordered. He crossed the open ground behind the wood out of the enemy's sight, entered the trees at their eastern side and worked his column slowly south-west through the undergrowth. He halted a little inside the southern edge without showing a man in the open."},
{"unitId":"red-3","x":1550,"y":400,"facingDeg":180,"formation":"line","strength":220,"morale":85,"fatigue":0,"ammo":100,"status":"active","continuing":{"kind":"hold"},"orders":[],"account":"Maj. von Reiter had no orders and held his squadron between the road and the wood."}
],
"observations":[],
"summary":"Turn 1 (0-20). Red's Line Battalion received its order at minute 2. It crossed the open ground north-east of the northern wood, out of any enemy's sight, entered the trees and worked its column south-west through them. It ends hidden just inside the wood's southern edge at about (950,820), tired from the going. Red's Vanguard Battalion stood in line by the high road at (1950,300) to draw the eye, but it is about 1.4 km from the nearest Blue troops, well beyond their sight. Blue's cavalry squadron received its order at minute 5, moved up to the river bank at (1100,1620) and watched the northern wood. The wood's edge is about 750 m off and the battalion inside it is concealed by the trees and beyond the squadron's 800 m sight in any case, so nothing was seen. No unit on either side saw an enemy this turn, and there was no fighting."}
